{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785993228872709001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"super-plant-liver","assignee":"","author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":12},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Iso Tester","body":"Analysis + fix in PR #51 (auto-merge enabled). WHICH CRITERIA should have caught it: E5 (testing, runs on story+task) and E6 (ac-text-quality, task-only) were best-positioned. E5 missed because 'thin-but-present coverage = PASS' had no concept of a mock that bypasses the new path; E6 missed because it treated the offline proving command as sufficient AND is routed task-only (never ran on the B5 STORY — so E5 is the actual catch for story cutovers). FIX (strengthen E5+E6 per direction): E5 gains PROXY-VALIDATION anti-pattern (defaulted path validated only via offline mock = MAJOR); E6 gains PROVING-COMMAND-EXERCISES-THE-CHANGE (cutover needs a live e2e AC; green offline + signed verdict necessary-but-not-sufficient); matching checklist bullets render into the finder prompt; B5-shaped eval recall cases + anti-over-fire good pair + offline presence test; docs/plan-review-gate.md cutover-DoD section; coaching via existing Pass-4 moves 7/9. Left E6 routing task-only to avoid broad over-fire (noted as possible follow-up). No index drift; 256 tests + eval-discipline pass. Will close on merge.","timestamp":1782529124282747001}],"created_at":1782512709817941001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0982f3bb-c3de-4243-b243-03dd0264ca06","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f12d-caa1-ea35-41b6"},{"link_uuid":"c014758b-d2c5-4c32-94d2-311204257f01","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0408-e8e5-f8aa-4d70"},{"link_uuid":"ad812981-23a4-4277-b8b0-f84e393428e1","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"72d5-79ec-9e2e-4a2b"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nROOT CAUSE of the B5 premature-close incident. The plan-review gate reviewed B5 (pout-gloss-hoop) and returned PASS, but did NOT flag a verification-completeness deficiency in B5's acceptance criteria: AC3 ('Integration tests cover claim+close pass/fail through the workflow path with intact signing') was satisfiable ENTIRELY by OFFLINE tests using canned agents that never call resolve_prompt — so the risky new behavior (the workflow plan-review verify/coach steps run against a LIVE model) had NO acceptance criterion requiring it to be exercised end-to-end. B5 shipped + closed (signed completion verdict) with the live plan-review claim gate broken (INDETERMINATE: 'prompt references undefined variable plan'). The completion verifier correctly certified AC-satisfaction-as-written; the gap is that the GATE that reviews PLANS did not catch that the AC could pass without exercising the changed, risky path.\n\n## Reproduction Steps\n\n1. Author a story (like B5) that CUTS OVER a gate/engine to a new code path and DEFAULTS to it.\n2. Write an AC that is satisfiable by OFFLINE/mocked tests only (no live / end-to-end exercise of the new path).\n3. Run rebar review-plan on the story. \n4. Observe: PASS, with no finding that the AC permits validating the risky behavior without ever running it (no live-verification / end-to-end-DoD requirement).\n5. The story ships; the live path is broken; nothing caught it until the path was hit by hand.\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\nEXPECTED: the plan-review gate's AC-quality / definition-of-done criteria (e.g. E6 ac-text-quality, F1, the T-series acceptance criteria) flag an AC whose verification can pass WITHOUT exercising the actually-changed risky behavior — especially for a cutover/migration that defaults to a new path. The coaching should push 'add a live/end-to-end acceptance criterion for the path you are defaulting to.'\n\nACTUAL: PASS with no such finding. The verification-completeness gap (offline-only validation of a path that needs live validation) escaped review, enabling B5 to close green while broken.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A plan-review criterion (new or strengthened, e.g. the AC-quality / proxy-validation dimension) flags an AC that can be satisfied WITHOUT exercising the changed risky behavior — i.e. mocked/offline-only verification of a path the story makes the default.\n- [ ] An eval/regression case encodes the B5-shaped scenario (a cutover defaulting to a new engine path with an offline-only AC) and asserts the gate surfaces the verification-completeness finding.\n- [ ] The coaching for that finding recommends adding a live/end-to-end DoD for the defaulted path.\n- [ ] Documented: a gate/engine cutover's DoD must include exercising the new path end-to-end against a live model (green offline tests + a passing completion verdict are necessary but not sufficient).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","72d5-79ec-9e2e-4a2b"],["relates_to","0408-e8e5-f8aa-4d70"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"72d5-79ec-9e2e-4a2b","parent_status_uuid":"f133cdfd-ecce-4fb9-863f-40ad55b52e88","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0895-14b6-1d03-49c5","ticket_type":"bug","title":"plan-review gate passed B5 without flagging that its AC allowed offline-only verification of a path that needed live validation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b2d44d6b-3388-4c11-8251-f0736c3f6318","0982f3bb-c3de-4243-b243-03dd0264ca06","c014758b-d2c5-4c32-94d2-311204257f01","a8691404-6fec-4b98-bf17-be2daccc9492","ad812981-23a4-4277-b8b0-f84e393428e1","296ebaa8-2355-4a4b-bf20-42801aad601e","532ba74a-7718-412a-b8be-8ac7788c2206","49bf4ab0-d69a-4a94-9ab3-9c77d6157387","f133cdfd-ecce-4fb9-863f-40ad55b52e88","4abbb7c3-d5ce-4552-a707-485dd8f540ea","d39d9e57-41e2-480e-81bb-db9639462bf8","a7b3e617-ab3d-4bd5-b209-cca001504320"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993228872709001,"uuid":"4f4b948f-a165-4e45-a20c-41413b2cf4db"}